<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karen people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karen are a group of related peoples speaking Karenic languages, living mainly in the hills of south-eastern Myanmar along the Thai border, with communities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. Many became Christians through 19th-century Baptist missions. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karen-national-union">Karen National Union</a> began an armed struggle for autonomy in 1949, one of the world's longest-running insurgencies, and hundreds of thousands of Karen have fled to camps in Thailand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karen-people.jpg" alt="Karen people" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: R. Lenz. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Karen_woman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
